# celestial_bridge's database: password hashes and every trade you have taken.
# It belongs on your machine, not in a repository.
celestial.db
celestial.db-wal
celestial.db-shm
celestial-backup-*.json

# The copy handed over for download, named for its build. Byte-identical to
# celestial_alpha_v2_22.html at that commit; the source is tracked and the
# history holds every build, so these are disposable.
#
# CORRECTION, AND IT COST A ROUND. The note that used to sit here said the
# delivered file should carry the SAME name every time so a new download
# "REPLACES the old one in Downloads". Chrome does not do that. It appends a
# counter — the screenshot that disproved it was opened from
# "celestial_alpha (44).html", forty-four copies deep, and the one on screen
# was an old one. A constant filename does not replace anything; it just
# produces an unreadable pile.
#
# So the build goes IN the filename, where sorting the folder by name puts the
# newest last and highest. And because a filename can still be mistaken, the
# running page now prints its build directly under the CAELUS wordmark, top of
# the sidebar and top of the phone header — the old marker was at the BOTTOM
# of the sidebar, below the fold on a laptop, which is why it never helped.
celestial_alpha_b*.html
celestial_alpha.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
